hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3065","**\nNarrated to us Yusuf ibn Wadih al-Hashimi, narrated to us al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ya'mur, who mentioned the hadith of Ibn Umar (RA) from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding the questioning of Jibril (AS) about Islam. He said:\n\n\Islam is that you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah"," and that you establish the prayer"," and give the zakah"," and perform Hajj and Umrah"," and that you perform ghusl from janabah"," and that you perfect your wudu"," and that you fast Ramadan.\""\n\nJibril (AS) then asked"," \""If I do all of that"," am I a Muslim?\""\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) replied"," \""Yes.\""\n\nJibril (AS) then said"," \""You have spoken the truth.\""\n\n---"""
"3066","Abdullah bin Sa'id al-Ashaj narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (RA), who said: \There is no one upon whom there are not two obligatory acts: Hajj and 'Umrah"," which are mandatory. Whoever performs more than that after fulfilling these two"," it is virtuous and voluntary.\"""""
"3067","Narrated to us Al-Ashajj, narrated to us Abu Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu az-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir (RA), who said:\n\There is no creation of Allah upon whom an obligatory 'Umrah is not due.\""\n\n---\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"3068","Abu Bakr (RA) said: This report indicates the weakening of the report of al-Hajjaj ibn Arta'ah, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir (RA), in which he said:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) was asked about whether the 'Umrah is obligatory, and he said: \No. If you perform the 'Umrah"," then it is better.\""\n\nThis was narrated by Bishr ibn Mu'adh"," who said: 'Amr ibn 'Ali told us"," who said: al-Hajjaj ibn Arta'ah told us"," from Ibn al-Munkadir"," from Jabir (RA).\n\nAbu Bakr (RA) commented: If Jabir (RA) had heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say that the 'Umrah is not obligatory"," he would not have contradicted the statement of the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nIn the report of Mansur"," from Abu Wa'il"," from al-Dabbi ibn Ma'bad"," in the story of 'Umar (RA)"," there is evidence that the 'Umrah is obligatory according to the view of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (RA).\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"3069","###\n Narrated to us by Yusuf bin Musa, who said: Narrated to us Jarir, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, who said: Ad-Dabbi bin Ma'bad said, \I was a Christian Arab. Then I embraced Islam"," and I was eager to perform Jihad. I found that both Hajj and 'Umrah were obligatory upon me. So I went to a man from my tribe named Hudaym bin Abdullah and said"," 'O Hanthah! I am eager to perform Jihad"," and I have found that Hajj and"""
